  "content": {
    "id": "p34-q13-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "13",
    "prompt": "[Auxiliary circle of a hyperbola]\n\nThe equation $(x+y)^2+(x-y)^2=a^2$ represents a circle when $a\\ne0$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p34-q13-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "By expanding then completing the square, find the radius of a circle in this form, in terms of $a$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$r=\\dfrac{|a|}{\\sqrt2}$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(x+y)^2+(x-y)^2&=a^2\\\\x^2+2xy+y^2+x^2-2xy+y^2&=a^2\\\\2x^2+2y^2&=a^2\\\\(x-0)^2+(y-0)^2&=\\frac{a^2}{2}\\\\r&=\\sqrt{\\frac{a^2}{2}}\\\\&=\\frac{|a|}{\\sqrt2}\\end{align*}$$\nThe centre is $(0,0)$. For positive $a$, the radius is $\\frac{a}{\\sqrt2}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 29
      },
      {
        "id": "p34-q13-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "What kind of curve is $(x+y)^2-(x-y)^2=a^2$? (Hint: expand and simplify.)",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "A hyperbola, $y=\\dfrac{a^2}{4x}$, when $a\\ne0$. For $a=0$, the relation is the two coordinate axes.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(x+y)^2-(x-y)^2&=a^2\\\\x^2+2xy+y^2-(x^2-2xy+y^2)&=a^2\\\\4xy&=a^2\\\\y&=\\frac{a^2}{4x}\\end{align*}$$\nFor $a\\ne0$, this is a rectangular hyperbola with the coordinate axes as asymptotes. For $a=0$, $xy=0$, so $x=0$ or $y=0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 21
      },
      {
        "id": "p34-q13-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Use DESMOS to sketch $(x+y)^2+(x-y)^2=a^2$ and $(x+y)^2-(x-y)^2=a^2$.\n\nCreate a slider for $a$ and experiment with values of $a$.\n\nhttps://www.desmos.com/calculator/luwgidnzzy\n\nWhat do you think the coordinates of the points of intersection are?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\left(\\dfrac a2,\\dfrac a2\\right)$ and $\\left(-\\dfrac a2,-\\dfrac a2\\right)$; the signs match.",
          "worked": "Enter both relations in DESMOS and create a slider for $a$. The intersections lie on $y=x$ at $\\left(\\frac a2,\\frac a2\\right)$ and $\\left(-\\frac a2,-\\frac a2\\right)$. Changing the sign of $a$ leaves both graphs unchanged. At $a=0$, the two listed points coincide at $(0,0)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 15
      },
      {
        "id": "p34-q13-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "Verify this algebraically.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Substitution gives $(4x^2-a^2)^2=0$, so the intersections are $\\left(\\dfrac a2,\\dfrac a2\\right)$ and $\\left(-\\dfrac a2,-\\dfrac a2\\right)$.",
          "worked": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p34-q13-d-expanded",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "right",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Expand and simplify both equations:",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "break"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "2x^2+2y^2=a^2,\\qquad 4xy=a^2.",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p34-q13-d-substitution",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "right",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "For ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "a\\ne0",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ", substitute ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "y=\\frac{a^2}{4x}",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " into the first equation:",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "break"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\begin{aligned}2x^2+2\\left(\\frac{a^2}{4x}\\right)^2&=a^2\\\\32x^4+2a^4&=16a^2x^2\\\\32x^4-16a^2x^2+2a^4&=0\\end{aligned}",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p34-q13-d-square",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "right",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Divide by 2 and recognise a perfect square:",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "break"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\begin{aligned}16x^4-8a^2x^2+a^4&=0\\\\(4x^2-a^2)^2&=0\\end{aligned}",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p34-q13-d-x",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "right",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Solve for ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "x",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ":",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "break"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\begin{aligned}4x^2-a^2&=0\\\\x^2&=\\frac{a^2}{4}\\\\x&=\\pm\\frac a2\\end{aligned}",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p34-q13-d-y",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "right",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Substitute into ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "y=\\frac{a^2}{4x}",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ":",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "break"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\begin{aligned}x=\\frac a2:\\quad y&=\\frac{a^2}{4(\\frac{a}{2})}=\\frac a2\\\\x=-\\frac a2:\\quad y&=\\frac{a^2}{4(-\\frac{a}{2})}=-\\frac a2\\end{aligned}",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "break"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Thus the signs match. For ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "a=0",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ", the first equation gives ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "x=y=0",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ", which also satisfies the second equation.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 50
      }
    ]
  },
